# Warbull — the cyber-minotaur, SECOND DRAFT: a fresh body authored against
# the owner's reference plate, docs/dev-notes/refs/warbull-reference.png
# (2026-09-27). The first draft was minotaur.blob scaled up, and the owner
# rejected it as the same creature as the existing bull brutes ("i wanted
# something like completely fresh take on it"). Nothing below comes from
# minotaur.blob or cyberdemon.blob: every number is measured off the plate or
# says why not.
#
# MEASURING THE PLATE. A front view, 696 x 936 px, a dark vignette backdrop.
# The flesh segments cleanly by warmth (r - b >= 9); the chrome drops out
# (neutral grey like the backdrop), so kit parts were read by eye. Scale: the
# horn tips (y 95) to the hoof soles (y 880) is 785 px, authored as 2.55 m,
# so ONE PIXEL IS 3.25 mm, and height = (880 - y_px) x 0.003248. The
# centreline is x 331 px. Measurements by row (full widths, metres):
#   y  138  horns, tip to tip   0.82   (2.41 m: the horns' outer sweep)
#   y  102  horn tips           x +-0.31, the top of the figure (2.53 m)
#   y  140  eyes                x +-0.123 (2.40 m)
#   y  174  muzzle              0.28   (2.29 m)
#   y  205  chin / trap line    (2.19 m): no visible neck at all
#   y  222  traps               0.74   (2.14 m)
#   y  258  deltoids, outer     0.96   (2.02 m)
#   y  330  armpits             (1.79 m); torso 0.55 below them
#   y  390  ribs                0.51   (1.59 m)
#   y  400-465  the RED CABLE BELT round the waist (1.56-1.35 m): kit
#   y  498  hips                0.63   (1.24 m)
#   y  516  crotch              (1.18 m)
#   y  534  thighs              0.32 each, centres x +-0.18
#   y  630  knees               0.24 each, centres x +-0.25 (0.81 m)
#   y  680  calves              0.21 each
#   y  720  ankle / brace top   0.13 each (0.52 m): chrome braces below
#   y  760-880  chrome pasterns and hooves, centres x +-0.27: kit + hoof
# The arm he HANGS (plate left, his right) runs deltoid (x -0.48, 2.02) ->
# elbow (-0.65, 1.62) -> wrist (-0.82, 1.40) -> claw tips (-0.90, 1.23),
# foreshortened: the forearm reaches forward. His other forearm is inside
# the chrome cannon (the launcher prop).
#
# ONE DEPARTURE FROM THE PLATE: the plate's cannon is on his LEFT arm. Every
# carry in the game (carry.ts) holds the prop in the RIGHT hand, so the gun
# arm is mirrored onto his right, and the hanging clawed arm is his left.
#
# WHAT READS AS HIM, from the plate, in order:
#   1. NO NECK. The traps rise to the jaw; the head sits down between them.
#   2. The HORNS: out sideways from the temples, then up, tips turning in.
#   3. A heavy V: 0.96 m deltoids over a 0.51 m waist, on LONG legs (the
#      crotch at 46% of his height) that splay out to wide-set hooves.
#   4. Long arms with a clawed hand hanging to the hip.
model warbull
  # To the horn tips (the plate's own scale choice above); the crown of the
  # skull is ~2.52, a hand under the 3 m room ceiling.
  height 2.55
  # Knees forward of the hip-ankle line (checked).
  stance humanoid

skeleton
  # The hip line at 1.21 (plate: hips 1.24, crotch 1.18): pelvis tail.
  root pelvis at 1.06 len=0.15
  # The torso stands UPRIGHT in the plate (no hunch): pitch 0-2.
  bone spine1 parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=1 len=0.22
  bone chest  parent=spine1 dir=up pitch=1 len=0.30
  bone spine2 parent=chest  dir=up pitch=0 len=0.12
  # The head PIVOTS at the neck tail (motion.ts's gaze nod turns the skull
  # about it). 2.09 is behind the jaw, the height his chin meets his traps
  # (2.19) less a jaw: a pivot deep in the traps swings the head like a
  # pendulum (the first draft's lesson, NOTES.md Task 5).
  bone neck   parent=spine2 dir=up pitch=0 len=0.25
  bone skull  parent=neck   dir=up pitch=0 len=0.40

  mirror
    # Shoulder joint at (0.36, 2.00): the deltoid ball (r 0.15) then reaches
    # the plate's 0.48 outer edge. From spine2's tail (1.84) that is 0.30 out
    # and 0.16 up.
    bone clavicle parent=spine2  side=0.06 dir=side tilt=30 len=0.32
    # Upper arm to the plate's elbow (0.65, 1.62): out 0.29, down 0.38.
    bone upperarm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=40 pitch=6 len=0.48
    # The forearm reaches FORWARD (the plate foreshortens it): pitch 35 puts
    # the wrist at z ~0.27, 1.32 m up, near the plate's 1.40.
    bone forearm  parent=upperarm dir=down tilt=28 pitch=30 len=0.40
    # A long clawed hand (plate: wrist 1.40 to claw tips 1.23).
    bone hand     parent=forearm  dir=down tilt=15 pitch=15 len=0.17
    # Hip joint x 0.18 (the plate's thigh centres), knee (0.25, 0.83).
    bone thigh    parent=pelvis side=0.19 dir=down tilt=9 pitch=8 len=0.38
    # The shin runs knee -> pastern: the braces and hooves hang off its
    # lower end, so it is LONG (0.66: knee 0.83 to the hoof top 0.17), and
    # the plate's hooves sit out at x 0.27.
    bone shin     parent=thigh  dir=down tilt=2 pitch=-6 len=0.66
    # Positions the hoof only (house pattern: horizontal, +z forward).
    bone foot     parent=shin   dir=fwd len=0.20
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # TORSO — the V. Widths are the plate's, depths are judgement (a front
  # plate has none): ~0.80 of width at the chest, a bodybuilder's barrel,
  # less at the waist.
  # ============================================================
  # Hip bowl: plate hips 0.63 at 1.24 (the thigh roots add the rest), its
  # bottom at 1.15 so the crotch opens near the plate's 1.18.
  blob torso on pelvis  at=1.00 r=0.18 wide=1.55 tall=0.50 deep=1.15 blend=0.020 offset=(0,0.03,0) core
  # Waist: the belt's 0.50-0.51 (1.35-1.56) plus the cables' ~1 cm. From
  # 0.45, not 0: a capsule's end cap hangs a radius past its end, and from
  # the hip line it filled the crotch down to 1.02 (the plate's is 1.18).
  bar  torso on spine1  from=0.45 to=1.00 r=0.19 wide=1.28 deep=1.10 blend=0.020 offset=(0,0,0.01)
  # Ribcage: 0.51 at the ribs, 0.55 under the armpits.
  bar  torso on chest   from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.21 wide=1.22 deep=1.12 blend=0.020 offset=(0,0,0.02)
  # Lats: the wide back that makes the V, behind the ribcage (a front plate
  # cannot see them; they carry the width up to the armpit).
  bar  torso on chest   from=0.35 to=1.15 r=0.20 wide=1.25 deep=0.85 blend=0.030 offset=(0,0,-0.07)
  # Pecs: a pair of broad FLAT slabs high on the chest, right under the
  # traps and deltoids (the plate's; a rounder, lower pair read as a belly).
  blob torso on chest   at=1.08 offset=(0.12,0,0.15) r=0.15 wide=1.25 tall=0.72 deep=0.52 blend=0.020 both
  # Abs: a raised slab down the front (the plate's ribbed six-pack; the
  # renderer cannot carry the grooves, the mass it can).
  bar  torso on spine1  from=0.20 to=1.30 offset=(0,0,0.12) r=0.10 wide=1.55 deep=0.42 blend=0.035
  # TRAPS: the no-neck beat. A pair of great mounds from the deltoids up to
  # the jaw: centre 0.17 out on the neck bone, top ~2.13 (the plate's 2.14).
  blob torso on neck    at=0.55 offset=(0.16,0,-0.03) r=0.21 wide=1.35 tall=1.20 deep=1.00 blend=0.025 both
  # Upper back behind them, so the traps read as one yoke from behind.
  blob torso on spine2  at=0.60 offset=(0,0.02,-0.10) r=0.22 wide=1.35 tall=0.80 deep=0.80 blend=0.030

  # Neck: short and thick, buried in the traps; fuses head to torso.
  bar  head on neck from=0.00 to=1.05 r=0.10 deep=1.10 blend=0.010

  # ============================================================
  # HEAD — the face block (below) is the skull; these add the bull.
  # ============================================================
  # MUZZLE: the plate's 0.28-wide snout at 2.29, forward of the face.
  blob head on skull at=0.52 offset=(0,0,0.19) r=0.10 wide=1.30 tall=0.85 deep=0.95 blend=0.012
  # HORNS: root at the temples (x 0.17, 2.45), out to the plate's widest
  # sweep (0.41 at 2.41) and up to the tips (0.31, 2.53), which turn back
  # IN. One bent tapered bar each: the chord runs root -> tip, and `bend`
  # (the control point's offset from the chord's midpoint) pulls it out and
  # down, so the horn leaves the skull sideways and hooks up at the end.
  # Endpoints: skull at t is y 2.09 + 0.40 t; t 0.90 -> 2.45.
  bar  head on skull from=0.90 to=0.90 offset=(0.16,0,0.02) tip=(0.15,0.06,0.05) bend=(0.22,-0.12,0.01) r=0.065 r2=0.014 blend=0.006 chamfer both color=2a1c14 gloss=0.4
  # Horn roots: a bony boss where each horn leaves the skull.
  blob head on skull at=0.88 offset=(0.15,0,0.02) r=0.06 blend=0.008 both color=3a2a20
  # EYES: glowing red beads under the brow (the plate's eyes are lit red),
  # spaced x +-0.12 at 2.41 (skull t 0.775). The face there curves back to
  # z 0.156 (sdBody probe with the beads removed), so a bead centred at
  # 0.152 (r 0.018) stands 1.4 cm proud: an eye in a socket, lit.
  blob head on skull at=0.775 offset=(0.12,0,0.143) r=0.018 blend=0.004 both color=ff2010 glow=0.9

  # ============================================================
  # ARMS — the deltoid ball is the arm's core. Girths off the plate: upper
  # arm ~0.26, forearm 0.22 at the elbow tapering to 0.14.
  # ============================================================
  blob arm on clavicle at=1.00 r=0.15 wide=1.00 blend=0.020 mirror core
  bar  arm on upperarm from=0.00 to=0.95 r=0.13 r2=0.11 blend=0.012 mirror
  bar  arm on forearm  from=0.00 to=0.95 r=0.11 r2=0.075 blend=0.010 mirror
  # The hand: a long palm and three claws (the plate's hanging hand).
  blob arm on hand at=0.30 r=0.06 wide=1.15 tall=1.40 deep=0.65 blend=0.008 mirror
  bar  arm on hand from=0.45 to=1.25 offset=(0.035,0,0.015) r=0.022 r2=0.008 blend=0.004 mirror color=2a1c14
  bar  arm on hand from=0.45 to=1.30 offset=(0,0,0.025) r=0.024 r2=0.008 blend=0.004 mirror color=2a1c14
  bar  arm on hand from=0.45 to=1.20 offset=(-0.035,0,0.015) r=0.022 r2=0.008 blend=0.004 mirror color=2a1c14

  # ============================================================
  # LEGS — long, heavy thighs, big calves, a slim lower shin that goes into
  # the chrome braces (kit), and a hoof.
  # ============================================================
  blob leg on thigh at=0.03 r=0.145 blend=0.020 mirror core
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.05 to=0.92 r=0.148 r2=0.12 blend=0.014 mirror
  blob leg on shin  at=0.00 r=0.12 blend=0.012 mirror
  # Calf: the plate's 0.21-0.24 bulge, carried behind the bone.
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.05 to=0.45 r=0.115 r2=0.10 deep=1.15 blend=0.012 mirror offset=(0,0,-0.02)
  # Lower shin down to the pastern: 0.13 at the brace top.
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.45 to=1.00 r=0.075 r2=0.065 blend=0.010 mirror
  # The hoof (dark keratin): the plate's natural hoof, a cloven block. The
  # kit shoes one of them in chrome.
  blob leg on foot at=0.35 offset=(0,-0.08,0) r=0.09 wide=1.20 tall=1.05 deep=1.30 blend=0.010 mirror color=2a1c14 gloss=0.5

# ============================================================
# FACE — the skull. A broad, deep bull cranium set forward on the pivot
# (headLead) and up to the eye line (headRise): the cranium centre sits at
# 2.09 + 0.45 x 0.40 + 0.09 = 2.36, between the brow (2.45) and the muzzle.
# ============================================================
face
  headRadius 0.15
  headWidth  1.05
  headHeight 1.18
  headDepth  1.40
  jawWidth   0.95
  jawHeight  0.90
  jawDrop    0.13
  jawJut     0.09
  noseLength 0.04
  noseWidth  1.20
  noseDrop   0.02
  browHeavy  0.03
  browRise   0.05
  headBlend  0.008
  headRise   0.07
  headLead   0.03

# Face decal: the plate's own head, cropped to a 200 px square (x 230-430,
# y 60-260), feathered to an oval round the face, resized to 512 (NOTES.md,
# "Face"): eyes, snout and snarl painted, the mass is the prims. Projection
# solved in head space of the fattest head prim (the cranium, centre
# (0, 2.350, 0.039), semi-axes 0.1575 x 0.177 x 0.210) on two features:
#   the eyes: image uv (0.31 / 0.69, 0.60) onto hs (+-0.762, 0.282), the
#     beads below at x +-0.12, y 2.40: scaleX 0.19 / 0.762 = 0.2493;
#   the mouth: image uv.y 0.325 onto y 2.225 (the plate's), hs.y -0.706:
#     scaleY 0.275 / 0.988 = 0.2783, centreY 0.60 - 0.282 x 0.2783 = 0.5215.
# Checks that fall out of it: the plate's chin lands at 2.19 and its crown at
# 2.51, both where the plate has them.
sheet
  image       warbull-face.png
  decal       1
  projScaleX  0.2493
  projScaleY  0.2783
  projCentreX 0.5
  projCentreY 0.5215
  eyeGlowAmp  2.2
  eyeGlowCut  0.55
  eyeGlowRedOnly 1

# Palette: the plate's hide is a dark chocolate brown (flesh sRGB ~48/36/25
# under its dim light, p90 59/47/37). Lifted for the game's hard key: the
# minotaur's measured brown rendered as a featureless dark mass (TASKS, its
# round 4), so the albedo sits well above the plate's lit value while
# keeping its hue, and the spec carries the wet muscle read.
palette
  baseColor     0.50 0.33 0.23
  deepColor     0.34 0.08 0.05
  charColor     0.08 0.05 0.04
  specIntensity 0.90
  specRoughness 0.20
  fresnelBoost  0.70
  translucency  0.30
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.08
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.012
  wetness       0.70
  mottleAmp     0.10
  mottleScale   1.8
  mottleColor   0.32 0.20 0.13
